---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy and terms | FORJD"
  description="FORJD uses your health data to show you your own training and recovery, and for nothing else. It never reaches an analytics or advertising service."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="label accent">Privacy and terms</span>
      <h1 class="display page-display">Your body's data<span class="dot">.</span><br />Your call<span class="dot">.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">The short version: we use your health data to show you your own training and recovery, and for nothing else.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec legal-sec">
    <div class="wrap legal-grid">
      <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <a href="#collect">What we collect</a>
        <a href="#use">How we use it</a>
        <a href="#never">What we never do</a>
        <a href="#control">Your controls</a>
        <a href="#credits">Data sources</a>
        <a href="#terms">Terms of use</a>
      </nav>
      <div class="doc">
        <div class="draft">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 8v5M12 16.5v.01M10.3 4.3 2.9 17.5A2 2 0 0 0 4.6 20.5h14.8a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 4.3a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z" stroke="#c9a03c" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
          <p><b>Draft, not legal text.</b> This page lays out structure and plain-language commitments. It needs review by someone qualified before launch.</p>
        </div>

        <section id="collect">
          <h2>What we collect</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Your account:</strong> email address, username, and the profile details you choose to add, such as your city.</li>
            <li><strong>Training:</strong> the workouts, sets, runs and programs you log in FORJD.</li>
            <li><strong>Health readings you connect:</strong> sleep, heart rate variability, resting heart rate and steps from Apple Health, Health Connect or WHOOP, only after you give permission on your phone.</li>
            <li><strong>Body composition:</strong> the InBody results you add.</li>
            <li><strong>Nutrition:</strong> the foods and meals you log.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="use">
          <h2>How we use it</h2>
          <p>
            To run the features you see: your history, charts, readiness score, FORJD Insights and, if you opt in, your
            place on your city's leaderboard. Each health reading is stored with the app or device it came from, so you
            can always see where a number originated.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="never">
          <h2>What we never do</h2>
          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Health data never reaches an analytics or advertising service.</strong> Not in the app, not on our servers, not while we're fixing a bug. We don't sell it, rent it or use it to target ads.</p>
          </div>
          <p>Data read from Apple Health and Health Connect is used only to provide FORJD's health and fitness features, as both platforms require.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="control">
          <h2>Your controls</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Export:</strong> download a copy of your account data from the app.</li>
            <li><strong>Delete:</strong> delete your account and its data from the app.</li>
            <li><strong>Disconnect:</strong> revoke Apple Health, Health Connect or WHOOP access at any time.</li>
            <li><strong>Public profile:</strong> choose what other athletes can see in privacy settings.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="credits">
          <h2>Data sources</h2>
          <p>City names and locations come from <strong>GeoNames</strong> (geonames.org), used under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="terms">
          <h2>Terms of use</h2>
          <p>To be written. It will cover accounts, subscriptions and renewals, acceptable use, and the fact that FORJD gives training information, not medical advice.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-display { font-size: clamp(42px, 6vw, 80px); }
  .legal-sec { padding-top: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px); }
  .draft { margin-top: 0; }
</style>
